# Line endings are part of this repository's contract, not a local preference.
#
# Git for Windows checks out with `core.autocrlf=true` by default (so do the
# GitHub Actions Windows runners), which rewrites every LF in the working tree
# to CRLF. Two things here are byte-exact artifacts that a checkout must not
# quietly rewrite:
#
#   * `crates/teksilo-corpus/corpus/index.json` — compact JSON holding exactly
#     one raw newline, the trailing one. Reproducing its bytes through the Rust
#     schema is a hard precondition of `cargo teksilo build-vectors`, which
#     refuses to run when the round trip differs.
#   * every file the corpus quotes — `cargo teksilo show` reconstructs those
#     line for line from chunk text that `tools/build_corpus.py` stored with
#     `\r` stripped (see its `split_lines`).
#
# Normalising the whole tree to LF is what makes a Windows checkout mean the
# same bytes as a Linux one. Without it both of the above compare a translated
# working tree against untranslated data and fail on Windows only.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Never newline-translate these, whatever the content heuristic decides.
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.webp binary
*.ttf  binary
